Privacy Policy for Ovum Hospitals App
Last updated: 26 July 2026

Ovum Hospitals (“we”, “our”, or “us”) built the Ovum Hospitals app ("App") to provide patients and caregivers easy access to information, appointments, and hospital services. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, retain, share, and protect your information, and how you can request deletion of your data. By downloading or using our App, you agree to the practices described below.

1. Information We Collect
Personal Information
Provided directly by you: Name, email address, phone number, date of birth, gender, and payment details (only when booking services).
Automatically collected: Usage data (features accessed, time spent), device information (model, OS version), and crash reports.
Location Data
With your permission, we may collect approximate location to suggest nearby facilities and services.

2. How We Use Your Information
App functionality: To manage registrations, appointments, bookings, service reminders, and payments.
Communications: Send notifications for appointments, updates, and offers.
Improvement & analytics: Understand app usage, diagnose bugs, and enhance user experience.
Legal compliance: Fulfill regulatory, audit, or legal obligations.
3. Data Retention
We retain your personal data only for as long as needed for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy, or as required by applicable law (including healthcare and tax/accounting rules in India).

Data type	Retention practice
Account / profile information (name, phone, email, date of birth, gender)	Kept while your account remains active. After account deletion is completed, we delete or anonymize this data within 30 days, unless a longer period is required by law.
Appointment and booking records	Retained for as long as needed to provide care continuity and to meet medical, legal, or regulatory record-keeping obligations. Where law allows, we may retain these records for up to 7 years (or such longer period as applicable regulations require), after which they are deleted or anonymized.
Payment-related information	Transaction and payment references are retained as needed for payment processing, refunds, dispute resolution, and financial/tax compliance (typically up to 7 years). We do not store full card numbers in the App; card payments are handled by our payment processor.
Usage, analytics, and crash data	Retained for a limited period for product improvement and diagnostics, generally up to 24 months, then deleted or aggregated so it no longer identifies you.
Location data	Used for the purpose collected (e.g., nearby facilities). We do not keep precise location histories longer than needed for that purpose; location permission can be revoked at any time in your device settings.
When data is no longer required, we delete it or irreversibly anonymize it so it can no longer be associated with you.

4. Data Deletion
You have the right to request deletion of your personal data associated with the Ovum Hospitals App.

How to request deletion
You can submit a data deletion request in any of the following ways:

In the App: Open Settings and use the available option to update or delete your account information, where provided.
By email: Send a deletion request to info@ovumhospitals.com with the subject line “Data Deletion Request – Ovum Hospitals App”. Include:
Your full name
Registered phone number (and email, if any)
A clear statement that you want your App account and related personal data deleted
Via our website: Contact us through https://www.ovumhospitals.com/ and request deletion of your App data.
What happens after you request deletion
We will acknowledge your request and aim to complete deletion (or confirm what cannot be deleted) within 30 days of verifying your identity.
Upon successful verification, we will delete or anonymize personal data we hold about you in connection with the App, including profile details and App account data, subject to the exceptions below.
We may retain certain information when we are legally required or permitted to do so—for example, appointment or medical-related records, payment/transaction records needed for compliance, fraud prevention, or dispute resolution. Such retained data will be limited to what is necessary and will not be used for other purposes.
After deletion, you may lose access to App features that depend on your account (appointments history, saved profiles, etc.).
If you only want to stop certain collection (for example, location or notifications), you can do so without deleting your account by changing permissions and notification settings on your device or in the App.

5. Sharing & Disclosure
We do not share or sell your personal data with third parties outside our organization, except:

With service providers engaged to perform App-related functions (e.g., payment processors, analytics).
If required by law or to protect rights and safety.
6. User Choices
You can:

Update or delete account information via the App settings, or by submitting a data deletion request as described in Section 4.
Enable or disable push notifications.
Manage or revoke location access permissions within your device’s settings.
7. Security Measures
We implement industry-standard safeguards (encryption, secure servers, limited access) to protect your personal data from unauthorized access, disclosure, or loss.

8. Children’s Privacy
The App is not intended for children under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from minors.

9. International Data Transfers
If you access the App outside India, be aware that your personal data may be processed on servers located in India in compliance with Indian data protection laws.

10. Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy. We will notify you via the App or email prior to changes taking effect. Continued use after notification means you accept the updated policy.

11. Contact Us
For any questions, concerns, or data deletion requests, please contact us at:

Website: https://www.ovumhospitals.com/
Email: info@ovumhospitals.com
By using the Ovum Hospitals app, you confirm that you agree to this Privacy Policy.
